# Health Care Data Analytics

## About
This project uses a healthcare dataset (`healthcare (1).xlsx`) with customer medical and hospitalisation details. It is used for data analysis in Excel.

## Dataset
The workbook has 3 sheets, linked by `Customer ID`:

| Sheet | Rows | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Customer Names | 2,335 | Customer ID and name |
| Medical Examinations | 2,335 | BMI, HbA1c, heart issues, transplants, cancer history, major surgeries, smoker status |
| Hospitalisation Details | 2,343 | Date, children, hospital charges, hospital tier, city tier, state ID |

## Key Columns
- **BMI**: body mass index (15.01 to 55.05)
- **HBA1C**: blood sugar measure (4.00 to 12.00)
- **charges**: hospital charges (563.84 to 63,770.43)
- **Hospital tier / City tier**: tier - 1, tier - 2, tier - 3
- **State ID**: 16 states (R1011 to R1026)

## Data Quality Notes
- Missing values are stored as `?` instead of blanks.
- 8 hospitalisation rows do not match any customer ID.
- `NumberOfMajorSurgeries` mixes numbers with the text "No major surgery".
- Yes/No values use inconsistent capitalisation (`yes`, `Yes`, `No`).

## How to Use
1. Download `healthcare (1).xlsx`.
2. Open it in Excel.
3. Clean the data (replace `?`, fix IDs, standardise Yes/No).
4. Join the sheets using `Customer ID` and analyse.

## Privacy
This dataset contains names and health information. Handle it as sensitive data.
